    "basis": "One 35 mm paving tile with two crates, a folded sack, an open wooden cage and a small hand plane. Preserve cage openings and separate timber/fabric/iron with 76k/26k independent bakes and compared1024/512 vs768/384 colour maps."
  },
  "reviewNotes": "PDF page4 and two 1000px source diagonals. Native datum17 mm, maximum 48.1464 mm; source paving probe[-13,-13,25.786873] mm. Closed-crate axes 73.25/53.75deg measured from side-plane normal histograms; cage excluded from that fit. Cage grain follows vertical meridians, retaining open slats and rings. Plane OBB center[2.782,2.431], angle 52.5deg, half widths[.887,5.179] mm; steel sole is separate from wooden arched handle. Mustard fabric sack uses a bounded ellipsoid and roughness .98. Occupied tile has no stand point; all metallic and roughness domains require decoded checks. Native stone-cap scans at25.1/25.2/25.3/25.4/25.5/25.7 mm consistently yield two large connected groups because the props join the surrounding paving; retain those measured groups rather than invent separate caps. Visual refinement: extend sack coverage to the sculpted lower hem and exclude the measured crate volumes so fabric cannot recolour wooden corners.",
